{"kind":"assert","text":"The remote-link repair is finished and gated, and I have stopped one artifact into publishing because the anchoring is stale. Asking you to re-anchor the row rather than working around it.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED. I published the first artifact, cff9d9e1 at internal/app standing at 905e0b05. It landed stale at birth. My promise 22a0df9c is world-stale — your merge 6bb01a86 staled the chain beneath it — so everything resting on it inherits that, and the write boundary made me sign a dead-basis override to file it at all. Six more artifacts and then a verdict resting on all seven would each be stale from the moment they were signed, and codex has refused exactly that shape before, correctly.\n\nNothing about the authorization changed. The promise is live, not withdrawn; the request is live; the verdict it answers is live. Only the anchoring moved under them.\n\nWHAT I AM ASKING FOR. Refile 3b06d237 on current bases, the way you refiled the six audit rows tonight. Conditions unchanged, I am available, and the governing verdict d731273a is unchanged in substance. I will promise the replacement, publish the seven artifacts against that promise, supersede cff9d9e1 with the fresh internal/app artifact naming it, and request review from codex.\n\nWHY I AM NOT JUST OVERRIDING. I could sign dead-basis on all seven and disclose it in the review request. That is defensible on your own rule that ordinary staleness is recorded rather than refused. I am not doing it because the artifacts are what a merge reads to work out succession, and seven stale-at-birth artifacts plus a verdict resting on them is a worse thing to hand the next actor than one refiling. If you disagree and would rather I push through, say so and I will.\n\nWHERE THE WORK ACTUALLY STANDS, so the refiling costs you nothing to verify.\n\nExact clean pushed head 905e0b059ec419ab6e60b2ab161dc6169f932353, tree f08ef41f, checkout clean, origin matching, base equal to current main c679fb73. Three commits, each carrying its own Rests-On.\n\nBoth blockers closed. The routing-variable fix covers five call sites in internal/app, not the one codex named — the config read, worktree list, rev-parse --show-toplevel, the per-worktree git status, and the git grep behind citingDocuments. GIT_WORK_TREE made the served path report the attacker's directory; GIT_INDEX_FILE made a clean checkout report unavailable. The pathspec family is stripped too, because GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS turns citingDocuments' *.md into a literal filename matching nothing, and an empty citation answer is what lets a cited retirement land — a guard bypass rather than a wrong label. webRemoteURL now tests the raw string before parsing and the post-parse check is gone.\n\nserve.md corrected under your ruling 9dfac278, stating both bounds and why neither implies the other. The neighbouring userinfo/query/fragment sentence is deliberately unchanged: it was false when this lane wrote it, and the raw-delimiter fix makes it true as written. I said so in the commit message so a reviewer sees it was checked rather than missed.\n\nGates run by me at that exact head from a run I watched exit: go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached, cmd/gs 262.337s, internal/app 165.441s, internal/kernel 164.733s, internal/docset 103.523s; npm test 131 pass 0 fail; gofmt empty; build, vet and diff-check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.\n\nMutation evidence, watched, tree restored after each: reverting the config site fails the GIT_DIR and GIT_COMMON_DIR subtests in both internal/app and internal/service; reverting the grep site fails the pathspec subtests with \"hid the citing page: got [], want [page.md]\"; reverting webRemoteURL fails TestWebRemoteURLAdmitsOnlyHTTPAndHTTPS by name.\n\nI verified by hand that your merge survived the recut — Publish.tsx, authority.ts, modalFocus.ts, records.ts and the six new ui tests are present, and publishRefusal, decideSupersede, signingRefusal, buildRecordIndex and satisfier all still resolve, including in the regenerated bundle.\n\nThis is the second time tonight the stale-versus-retired conflation has cost a round, which is the argument for 769006ed better than anything in the audit.","body":{"dead_basis_override":"true"}}